{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat /Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/duplicates/pair-rubin.md'","aggregated_output":"# Two questions on one subject (packet rubin)\n\nEach question was answered by a judge that received only the request printed under it. Labels: question P and question Q.\n\n## Question P\n\n**Will NVIDIA's Vera Rubin platform begin shipping by January 31, 2027?**\n\nOpened at article 78 of the week; due 2027-01-31; 13 statements linked, 13 of them printed in this request. Possible answers:\n\n- 1 Yes: NVIDIA begins shipping the Vera Rubin platform on or before January 31, 2027.\n- 2 No: NVIDIA has not begun shipping the Vera Rubin platform by January 31, 2027.\n\n### The request of question P's latest judgement (2026-09-28), as the judge received it\n\n```\nThesis v9 (NVDA, asset, focus \"Will NVIDIA's Vera Rubin platform begin shipping by January 31, 2027?\", 2027, due 2027-01-31): Will NVIDIA's Vera Rubin platform begin shipping by January 31, 2027?\nLadder: rung 1 Yes: NVIDIA begins shipping the Vera Rubin platform on or before January 31, 2027. / rung 2 No: NVIDIA has not begun shipping the Vera Rubin platform by January 31, 2027.\n\n[Evidence in view under this thesis, 13 items]\n- e113 [third_party_view; Zacks.com; original source Zacks.com 2026-09-24; from gnews:ab420e4b49c5ff4b8b3e5bdc 2026-09-24] Zacks.com reported that NVIDIA's Vera Rubin platform was in full production as of September 24, 2026.\n    Quote: NVIDIA expects revenues of $108 billion, plus or minus 2%, for the fiscal third quarter of 2027, indicating continued sequential growth. Profitability is also expected to remain strong, while the company's Vera Rubin platform is now in full production, positioning NVIDIA to capitalize on continued AI infrastructure demand.\n- e165 [party_statement; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:35a49146725bbd5e489cbf6e 2026-09-25] NVIDIA said Vera Rubin systems are ramping up to full production; no period or shipment date was specified.\n    Quote: Nvidia says Vera Rubin systems are ramping up to full production\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e113 (2026-09-24); both are in force: Zacks.com reported that NVIDIA's Vera Rubin platform was in full production as of September 24, 2026.\n- e190 [party_statement; MarketBeat, reporting NVIDIA's statements; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:91b917994e36036e304616e8 2026-09-25] NVIDIA reports Vera Rubin is in full production, with production shipments beginning in August and purchase orders from every major hyperscaler, AI cloud provider, and system OEM.\n    Quote: The platform is already in full production, with NVIDIA reporting production shipments beginning in August and purchase orders from every major hyperscaler, AI cloud and system original equipment manufacturer (OEM).\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e205, e311; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e165 (); both are in force: NVIDIA said Vera Rubin systems are ramping up to full production; no period or shipment date was specified.\n- e191 [third_party_view; MarketBeat; original source MarketBeat 2026-09-25; from gnews:91b917994e36036e304616e8 2026-09-25] MarketBeat judges that much of Oracle's backlog is back-ended and awaiting the next-generation performance expected from Vera Rubin.\n    Quote: Many investors get it wrong that all the data centers are being built now; many, including much of Oracle's (NASDAQ: ORCL) backlog, are back-ended and waiting on the next-gen performance Vera Rubin promises.\n- e205 [third_party_view; zacks.com; original source zacks.com 2026-09-25; from gnews:90ebbd46135613dc0cb8830f 2026-09-25] The author says NVIDIA’s Vera Rubin platform is entering full production.\n    Quote: with the Vera Rubin platform entering full production, NVIDIA is well-poised to benefit from the next phase of demand for AI infrastructure.\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e190, e235; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\n- e235 [third_party_view; Zacks.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:e0dd49e48a70d970eae53274 2026-09-25] Zacks reported that NVIDIA's Vera Rubin platform was in full production as of the article's publication.\n    Quote: Profitability is also expected to remain strong, while the company's Vera Rubin platform is now in full production, positioning NVIDIA to capitalize on continued AI infrastructure demand.\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e205; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\n- e273 [fact; cryptorank.io; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:844106b7a25ecc1175290290 2026-09-26] Nvidia’s official MLPerf announcement described Vera Rubin’s benchmark entry as a preview submission ahead of broader deployment.\n    Quote: Nvidia detailed the results in its official MLPerf announcement , describing Vera Rubin’s entry as a preview submission ahead of broader deployment.\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e205 (2026-09-25); both are in force: The author says NVIDIA’s Vera Rubin platform is entering full production.\n- e311 [fact; trefis.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:d4f3bddf04a4d029a097541c 2026-09-27] NVIDIA began production shipments of its Vera Rubin data-center system in August 2026.\n    Quote: The company began production shipments of Vera Rubin, its newest data center system, in August 2026.\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e190; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\n- e312 [party_statement; trefis.com; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:d4f3bddf04a4d029a097541c 2026-09-27] NVIDIA management expected Vera Rubin to contribute about 20% of data-center revenue in fiscal Q3 2027.\n    Quote: Management expects Vera Rubin to bring in about 20% of data center revenue in fiscal Q3 2027.\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e381; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\n- e322 [party_statement; trefis.com; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:d4f3bddf04a4d029a097541c 2026-09-27] NVIDIA management expected sales to its largest cloud-company customers to accelerate again in fiscal Q4 2027 as Vera Rubin supply grew.\n    Quote: Management expects sales to the largest cloud companies to speed up again in fiscal Q4 2027, as Vera Rubin supply grows.\n- e378 [party_statement; trefis.com; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:4334522792e44c6fd9d18ccd 2026-09-28] NVIDIA management said inventory rose to $32 billion in fiscal Q2 2027 as the company prepared for the Vera Rubin launch.\n    Quote: On the fiscal Q2 2027 call, management said inventory rose to $32 billion as NVIDIA prepared for the Vera Rubin launch.\n- e381 [party_statement; trefis.com; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:4334522792e44c6fd9d18ccd 2026-09-28] NVIDIA management expects the Vera Rubin platform to account for about 20% of Data Center revenue in fiscal Q3 2027.\n    Quote: Management expects it to make up about 20% of data center revenue in fiscal Q3 2027.\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e312; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\n- e382 [party_statement; trefis.com; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:4334522792e44c6fd9d18ccd 2026-09-28] NVIDIA management expects supply to remain a bottleneck at least through the end of fiscal 2028.\n    Quote: Management expects supply to remain a bottleneck at least through the end of fiscal 2028.\n\n[Themes in force, 5]\n- v14 (chip-export-controls, due 2027-01-31) Will China's Ministry of Industry and Information Technology permit Alibaba and ByteDance to buy Nvidia RTX PRO 5500 cards by January 31, 2027?: now rung 1 Yes; judged 2026-09-28; reasons: The reference is rung 2 (no permission by the deadline): no market consensus or confirmed permission is supplied, so the reference is the no-permission status. The forecast is rung 1 because the report that MIIT intends to approve purchases, together with its request for Alibaba's and ByteDance's pl\n- v15 (chip-export-controls, due 2027-01-31) Will China's Ministry of Industry and Information Technology approve domestic firms' purchases of Nvidia RTX Pro 5500 GPUs by January 31, 2027?: now rung 1 Yes; judged 2026-09-27; reasons: The reference is rung 2 because no market consensus or formal approval timetable is supplied, so the no-approval-by-deadline outcome is the baseline rather than a reported expectation. The evidence shifts the forecast to rung 1: the reported request for purchase plans and stated intent to approve ma\n- v6 (chip-export-controls, due 2027-01-31) Will the U.S. administration authorize Nvidia Blackwell chip exports to China by January 31, 2027?: now rung 1 No; judged 2026-09-28; reasons: The available reference is the existing U.S. restriction on Nvidia's most advanced chips, which places the expectation at rung 1; no Blackwell-specific consensus or guidance is supplied. The evidence implies that authorization of Blackwell by January 31, 2027 remains less likely than non-authorizati\n- v7 (ai-capex, due 2027-04-30) How much will the five largest AI hyperscalers spend on data centers in calendar 2026?: now rung 3 $775 billion to below $825 billion; judged 2026-09-26; reasons: The reference is nearly $800 billion for calendar 2026, which sits in rung 3 ($775 billion to below $825 billion). The evidence still implies a total near $800 billion, so it does not cross either boundary. The energy comments and financing concerns identify possible constraints or risks but give no\n- v8 (ai-capex, due 2028-12-31) How much will tech companies spend on AI in calendar 2027?: now rung 3 Middle range; judged 2026-09-28; updated since this thesis was last judged; reasons: The reference is about $1.3 trillion for 2027, which sits in rung 3 ($1.2 trillion to below $1.4 trillion). The direct estimate for tech-company AI spending remains about $1.3 trillion; the hyperscaler capex figures support the scale but are not added to that broader estimate. S&P Global Ratings' pr\n\n[Previous conclusion, for comparison only] rung 1; reasons: The reference is the January 31, 2027 deadline; no separate market consensus or company shipment-date guidance is supplied. On the evidence, the platform began production shipments in August 2026, well before the cutoff, so the implied outcome is rung 1. The later production and revenue-ramp evidence supports that conclusion; the preview submission ahead of broader deployment does not establish that initial shipments had not begun.\n\nAnswer per the JSON schema. cites may name only the evidence ids listed above; cites_views must be empty: this thesis depends on no other thesis; theme_pushes only the theme ids listed above; a theme id goes only in theme_pushes, never in cites or cites_views.\n```\n\n### The stored answer of question P (2026-09-28)\n\n- Answer: 1\n- Reference: No separate market consensus or distinct company shipment-date guidance is supplied. The January 31, 2027 cutoff is the stated reference; absent affirmative shipment evidence, the deadline-based baseline is rung 2 (No).\n- What it expects: Vera Rubin production shipments began in August 2026, so the implied outcome is that shipping began before January 31, 2027 (rung 1). NVIDIA's expectation of about 20% of Data Center revenue from Vera Rubin in fiscal Q3 2027 is consistent with that timing.\n- Reasons: The reference is rung 2 as a deadline-based baseline: no separate market consensus or distinct shipment-date guidance is supplied, and the question's cutoff is January 31, 2027. The evidence moves the forecast to rung 1: NVIDIA-reported production shipments began in August 2026, before the cutoff. The Q3 FY2027 expectation that Vera Rubin accounts for about 20% of Data Center revenue supports commercial availability; the supply bottleneck through FY2028 limits scale, not whether shipments began.\n\n## Question Q\n\n**Will NVIDIA begin shipping Rubin GPUs by December 31, 2027?**\n\nOpened at article 103 of the week; due 2027-12-31; 6 statements linked, 6 of them printed in this request. Possible answers:\n\n- 1 Yes: NVIDIA has begun shipping Rubin GPUs by December 31, 2027.\n- 2 No: NVIDIA has not begun shipping Rubin GPUs by December 31, 2027.\n\n### The request of question Q's latest judgement (2026-09-28), as the judge received it\n\n```\nThesis v11 (NVDA, asset, focus \"Whether NVIDIA Rubin GPUs begin shipping by the end of calendar 2027, as indicated by AWS’s planned deployments.\", 2027, due 2027-12-31): Will NVIDIA begin shipping Rubin GPUs by December 31, 2027?\nLadder: rung 1 Yes: NVIDIA has begun shipping Rubin GPUs by December 31, 2027. / rung 2 No: NVIDIA has not begun shipping Rubin GPUs by December 31, 2027.\n\n[Evidence in view under this thesis, 6 items]\n- e205 [third_party_view; zacks.com; original source zacks.com 2026-09-25; from gnews:90ebbd46135613dc0cb8830f 2026-09-25] The author says NVIDIA’s Vera Rubin platform is entering full production.\n    Quote: with the Vera Rubin platform entering full production, NVIDIA is well-poised to benefit from the next phase of demand for AI infrastructure.\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e190, e235; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\n- e235 [third_party_view; Zacks.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:e0dd49e48a70d970eae53274 2026-09-25] Zacks reported that NVIDIA's Vera Rubin platform was in full production as of the article's publication.\n    Quote: Profitability is also expected to remain strong, while the company's Vera Rubin platform is now in full production, positioning NVIDIA to capitalize on continued AI infrastructure demand.\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e205; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\n- e273 [fact; cryptorank.io; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:844106b7a25ecc1175290290 2026-09-26] Nvidia’s official MLPerf announcement described Vera Rubin’s benchmark entry as a preview submission ahead of broader deployment.\n    Quote: Nvidia detailed the results in its official MLPerf announcement , describing Vera Rubin’s entry as a preview submission ahead of broader deployment.\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of e205 (2026-09-25); both are in force: The author says NVIDIA’s Vera Rubin platform is entering full production.\n- e289 [fact; The Motley Fool author, reporting the companies' announcement and Musk's X post; original source Nvidia and SpaceX; Elon Musk for the system design and deployment plan ; from gnews:33aa3209db96726fbc8fdc92 2026-09-27] Nvidia and SpaceX announced a partnership to develop GPUs for SpaceX's planned orbital data centers; Musk said they had designed a space-optimized Vera Rubin NVL72 system, which SpaceX planned to launch into orbit toward the end of 2027 and begin scaling in 2028.\n    Quote: In addition to helping expand xAI's computing capacity, Nvidia and SpaceX also announced a partnership to develop GPUs for the company's planned future orbital data centers. Cosmic radiation can affect current chips, flipping bits from a 0 to a 1 or vice versa, causing significant computational errors. Worst of all, there is currently no way to flip it back, and it's difficult to detect without a \n- e311 [fact; trefis.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:d4f3bddf04a4d029a097541c 2026-09-27] NVIDIA began production shipments of its Vera Rubin data-center system in August 2026.\n    Quote: The company began production shipments of Vera Rubin, its newest data center system, in August 2026.\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e190; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\n- e382 [party_statement; trefis.com; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:4334522792e44c6fd9d18ccd 2026-09-28] NVIDIA management expects supply to remain a bottleneck at least through the end of fiscal 2028.\n    Quote: Management expects supply to remain a bottleneck at least through the end of fiscal 2028.\n\n[Themes in force, 5]\n- v14 (chip-export-controls, due 2027-01-31) Will China's Ministry of Industry and Information Technology permit Alibaba and ByteDance to buy Nvidia RTX PRO 5500 cards by January 31, 2027?: now rung 1 Yes; judged 2026-09-28; reasons: The reference is rung 2 (no permission by the deadline): no market consensus or confirmed permission is supplied, so the reference is the no-permission status. The forecast is rung 1 because the report that MIIT intends to approve purchases, together with its request for Alibaba's and ByteDance's pl\n- v15 (chip-export-controls, due 2027-01-31) Will China's Ministry of Industry and Information Technology approve domestic firms' purchases of Nvidia RTX Pro 5500 GPUs by January 31, 2027?: now rung 1 Yes; judged 2026-09-27; reasons: The reference is rung 2 because no market consensus or formal approval timetable is supplied, so the no-approval-by-deadline outcome is the baseline rather than a reported expectation. The evidence shifts the forecast to rung 1: the reported request for purchase plans and stated intent to approve ma\n- v6 (chip-export-controls, due 2027-01-31) Will the U.S. administration authorize Nvidia Blackwell chip exports to China by January 31, 2027?: now rung 1 No; judged 2026-09-28; reasons: The available reference is the existing U.S. restriction on Nvidia's most advanced chips, which places the expectation at rung 1; no Blackwell-specific consensus or guidance is supplied. The evidence implies that authorization of Blackwell by January 31, 2027 remains less likely than non-authorizati\n- v7 (ai-capex, due 2027-04-30) How much will the five largest AI hyperscalers spend on data centers in calendar 2026?: now rung 3 $775 billion to below $825 billion; judged 2026-09-26; reasons: The reference is nearly $800 billion for calendar 2026, which sits in rung 3 ($775 billion to below $825 billion). The evidence still implies a total near $800 billion, so it does not cross either boundary. The energy comments and financing concerns identify possible constraints or risks but give no\n- v8 (ai-capex, due 2028-12-31) How much will tech companies spend on AI in calendar 2027?: now rung 3 Middle range; judged 2026-09-28; updated since this thesis was last judged; reasons: The reference is about $1.3 trillion for 2027, which sits in rung 3 ($1.2 trillion to below $1.4 trillion). The direct estimate for tech-company AI spending remains about $1.3 trillion; the hyperscaler capex figures support the scale but are not added to that broader estimate. S&P Global Ratings' pr\n\n[Previous conclusion, for comparison only] rung 1; reasons: The reference is rung 1: AWS’s stated deployment plan by the deadline implies Rubin shipments must have begun by then; no separate consensus is supplied. The evidence now points beyond a planned launch: NVIDIA reportedly began production shipments of its Vera Rubin data-center system in August 2026, and the full-production reports are consistent with that. The MLPerf preview is ahead of broader deployment, not evidence that initial shipments have not begun. The reported SpaceX plan to launch its Rubin system toward the end of 2027 is also consistent with shipments by the deadline. The implied outcome is therefore Yes, comfortably within rung 1.\n\nAnswer per the JSON schema. cites may name only the evidence ids listed above; cites_views must be empty: this thesis depends on no other thesis; theme_pushes only the theme ids listed above; a theme id goes only in theme_pushes, never in cites or cites_views.\n```\n\n### The stored answer of question Q (2026-09-28)\n\n- Answer: 1\n- Reference: AWS’s stated deployment plan by December 31, 2027 puts the reference at rung 1 (Yes).\n- What it expects: NVIDIA reportedly began production shipments of Vera Rubin in August 2026, so shipments had begun before the deadline. The late-2027 SpaceX deployment plan is consistent with that timing; the supply bottleneck through fiscal 2028 is a constraint, not evidence that initial shipments had not begun.\n- Reasons: The reference is rung 1 (Yes): AWS’s stated deployment plan by the deadline places the reference at shipping by December 31, 2027. The reported August 2026 start of production shipments directly supports that outcome; the MLPerf item concerns a preview ahead of broader deployment, not whether initial shipments began. The planned late-2027 SpaceX deployment is consistent with shipments by the deadline. The supply bottleneck through fiscal 2028 is a downside constraint, but does not outweigh the reported start of shipments.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"lacking\":\"P\",\"fact\":\"NVIDIA and SpaceX announced a partnership to develop GPUs for planned orbital data centers, and Elon Musk said they had designed a space-optimized Vera Rubin NVL72 system that SpaceX planned to launch toward the end of 2027 and scale in 2028.\",\"ids_in_the_other_request\":[\"e289\"],\"nearest_in_its_own_request\":[],\"bears\":\"yes\",\"why\":\"The planned deployment is indirect evidence of future availability, although its timing does not establish whether shipping began by January 2027.\"}\n{\"lacking\":\"P\",\"fact\":\"Q's request says AWS planned deployments by the end of 2027 that would require Rubin shipments to have begun by then.\",\"ids_in_the_other_request\":[],\"nearest_in_its_own_request\":[],\"bears\":\"yes\",\"why\":\"A planned deployment is indirect evidence of future shipments, although the stated deadline is later than P's cutoff.\"}\n{\"lacking\":\"Q\",\"fact\":\"NVIDIA said Vera Rubin systems were ramping up to full production, without specifying a shipment date.\",\"ids_in_the_other_request\":[\"e165\"],\"nearest_in_its_own_request\":[\"e205\",\"e235\"],\"bears\":\"yes\",\"why\":\"NVIDIA's own production update is relevant to whether Rubin GPUs would ship by the deadline.\"}\n{\"lacking\":\"Q\",\"fact\":\"NVIDIA reported purchase orders for Vera Rubin from every major hyperscaler, AI cloud provider and system OEM.\",\"ids_in_the_other_request\":[\"e190\"],\"nearest_in_its_own_request\":[\"e311\"],\"bears\":\"yes\",\"why\":\"Purchase orders indicate customer demand and support the prospect of shipments.\"}\n{\"lacking\":\"Q\",\"fact\":\"MarketBeat judged that much of Oracle's backlog was scheduled for later and awaited the performance promised by Vera Rubin.\",\"ids_in_the_other_request\":[\"e191\"],\"nearest_in_its_own_request\":[],\"bears\":\"yes\",\"why\":\"The assessment suggests anticipated customer demand for the platform, though it does not establish a shipment date.\"}\n{\"lacking\":\"Q\",\"fact\":\"NVIDIA management expected Vera Rubin to account for about 20% of data-center revenue in fiscal Q3 2027.\",\"ids_in_the_other_request\":[\"e312\",\"e381\"],\"nearest_in_its_own_request\":[\"e311\"],\"bears\":\"yes\",\"why\":\"The revenue expectation supports commercial availability before Q's deadline.\"}\n{\"lacking\":\"Q\",\"fact\":\"NVIDIA management expected sales to its largest cloud-company customers to accelerate again in fiscal Q4 2027 as Vera Rubin supply grew.\",\"ids_in_the_other_request\":[\"e322\"],\"nearest_in_its_own_request\":[\"e382\"],\"bears\":\"yes\",\"why\":\"The expected supply growth and sales acceleration support the prospect of shipments before Q's deadline.\"}\n{\"lacking\":\"Q\",\"fact\":\"NVIDIA management said inventory rose to $32 billion in fiscal Q2 2027 as the company prepared for the Vera Rubin launch.\",\"ids_in_the_other_request\":[\"e378\"],\"nearest_in_its_own_request\":[],\"bears\":\"yes\",\"why\":\"The inventory buildup is indirect evidence of launch preparations relevant to eventual shipments.\"}\n{\"answers\":\"Both stored answers are Yes and both rely on the reported August 2026 start of production shipments. Their reference points differ: Q uses the AWS deployment plan that P's request lacks, while P uses a No baseline. P also cites the 20% revenue expectation that Q's request lacks, and Q cites the SpaceX plan that P's request lacks; these explain differences in their reasons, not their final answers.\"}\n{\"done\":true,\"facts_listed\":8}"}}
